{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never asserts recv_buf_valid so trace ends with TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received and FAIL 0xdead instead of a received byte. Expected recv_state to advance through data-bit states 2-9 to state 10 to latch recv_pattern into recv_buf_data, but it remains stuck. Root cause is line 99 in picosoc/simpleuart.v `recv_state <= recv_state + 0;` in the default case which never increments, making state 10 unreachable.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 			default: begin
 				if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 					recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
-					recv_state <= recv_state + 0;
+					recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP: uart timeout — loopback byte 0xa5 received with recv_buf_valid asserted"}

